extraction_notes: "WB9 South America 2 printed 144-146 (cache p144-p146, page_offset 0); the introduction starts at the foot of 144, the stat block and abilities are on 145, the skill list ends on 146. Printed 145 read off a 110 dpi render; it agrees with the OCR on every number (the OCR''s 8.D.C. is S.D.C.). No equinoid class was in production on 2026-09-25. || XP: the Larhold Barbarian, Neo-Human and Equinoid ladder on printed 192, read off a render, as briefed; the book prints a ladder for the race and the R.C.C. is played on its own, so it is stored. || ATTRIBUTES as printed: I.Q. 3D6, M.E. 3D6+6, M.A. 3D6, P.S. 3D6+18, P.P. 3D6+6, P.E. 3D6+10, P.B. 4D6, Spd 1D6x10+80 running and flying. || POOLS: hit points P.E. x3 plus 2D6 per level. S.D.C. 1D4x100 plus skill bonuses, stored as sdc_base because the R.C.C. is the character''s whole class (the flying-tiger precedent), so no men_of_arms line. The M.D.C. line prints only the telekinetic force field (60 + 10 per level); it is not a natural M.D.C. body, so no mdc_base and the field is a special ability, as the flying-tiger''s is. P.P.E. 2D6. Horror Factor 8. || PSIONICS: the book names no tier. Stored as major (judgement): six powers from two categories and no growth is the major-psionic allotment, and the page''s own abilities are its only super powers; a master reading would change its save threshold. Six from Sensitive or Physical in any mix; no powers_per_level, as printed. I.S.P. 2D6x10+10 plus M.E., +2D6 per level. Sky running, psi-bow and the force field are special abilities with their I.S.P. costs, not catalog psionics. || BONUSES: ''add one melee attack per round'' (Combat line) is combat attacks 1; +2 initiative, +1 strike and parry, +1 roll with impact, +2 pull punch, +1 save vs magic (spell_magic), +4 vs Horror Factor, all unconditional and stored. The psi-bow''s +2 to strike is conditional and prose. Prowl -10% is a penalty on one skill, in side_effects rather than folded into any skill. || SKILLS: Language and Literacy: Spanish (98%) is Language: Spanish 98 plus Literacy: Native Language 98. Language one of choice +15 as a choice of Quechua, Aymara or Language: Other. Radio Basic is Radio: Basic 45+10 = 55. Tracking (animals and humans; +10%) is granted as both catalog rows, Tracking (people) 25+10 = 35 and Track & Trap Animals 20+10 = 30 (judgement: the book names both quarries and the catalog splits them). Wilderness Survival 30+10 = 40. W.P. Archery and Targeting is W.P. Archery. W.P. one of choice. Hand to Hand: Expert to Martial Arts for one other skill (costs martial_arts 1); no Assassin offered. || RELATED: eight, plus two at levels 3 and 6, one at 8, 10 and 14. Communications and Domestic +5, Military +5, Technical +10, Wilderness +10; Medical First Aid and Paramedic only; Physical any except Acrobatics and Climbing; Pilot any except power armor and robots (Robots & Power Armor, Air Assault Armor and every Robot Combat row excluded, as the flying-tiger did, plus Motorcycles & Snowmobiles because the Vulnerabilities line forbids motorcycles), with the custom-vehicle limit in the note; Electrical, Espionage, Mechanical, Pilot Related, Rogue, Science and W.P. any. No Horsemanship is offered: the book''s Pilot limit and a horse-bodied rider make it a judgement to leave out. || SECONDARY: ''three secondary skills at levels one and four'', read as three at each (count 3, +3 at level 4), the rune-warrior reading of the same wording in this book; same limits without the bonuses. || EQUIPMENT: Custom Barding (90 M.D.C.) has NO gear row - the book gives it no stat block and nothing in the catalog is this armor (cavalry-armor-barding and tw-animal-barding are other books'' horse armor for a mount, not a Psi-Taur''s own armor) - so it is not stored and is named in side_effects. One energy weapon of choice as a choice led by the Achilles Lightbringer and IP-7; four extra E-clips (e-clip x4); hand radio as walkie-talkie; gas mask, survival kit, bedroll, one week''s rations and survival knife. || MONEY: 2D6x100 credits. || Cybernetics: no line printed; nothing stored."
