## Lore

The Psi-Taur was never meant to exist. A renegade Achilles researcher, working
in secret with mostly human genes, tried to recreate the monsters of myth, and
dozens of human subjects died before his work was uncovered and he met a
convenient accident. One strain had already taken: a furred human torso on a
horse''s body, with a crest of hair like a natural mohawk.

The equinoid had a horse''s speed and strength, a human mind and remarkable
psionic power, so the project quietly kept breeding it. Like the other mutants,
the Psi-Taurs broke out of the laboratories and helped build the mutant
homeland.

They can run on empty air, form bows and arrows of pure mental energy, and wrap
themselves in force fields that let them strike with mega-damage. Most young
Psi-Taurs serve full time in the Achilles Army; the rest work as scouts,
messengers and bodyguards, in a mostly friendly rivalry with the Blood Riders
and the gauchos.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'equinoid');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'equinoid';

